227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 84 0 R
/T (The Zimbabwean real estate market has witnessed notable price increase trends over the past few years, driven by a combination of factors that reflect both opportunities and challenges in the sector.)
/E (The Zimbabwean real estate market has witnessed notable price increase trends over the past few years, driven by a combination of factors that reflect both opportunities and challenges in the sector.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 84 0 R
/T (Economic Factors:    - Hyperinflation: Zimbabwe has grappled with hyperinflation, which has significantly eroded the value of the local currency. This has led to a surge in property prices as real estate is often considered a hedge against inflation.    - Foreign Currency Transactions: Many high-end properties in Zimbabwe are priced and transacted in foreign currencies such as the United States Dollar \(USD\) or South African Rand \(ZAR\). This has led to price increases as the local currency's instability persists.)
/E (Economic Factors:    - Hyperinflation: Zimbabwe has grappled with hyperinflation, which has significantly eroded the value of the local currency. This has led to a surge in property prices as real estate is often considered a hedge against inflation.    - Foreign Currency Transactions: Many high-end properties in Zimbabwe are priced and transacted in foreign currencies such as the United States Dollar \(USD\) or South African Rand \(ZAR\). This has led to price increases as the local currency's instability persists.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 84 0 R
/T ( Urbanisation and Population Growth:    - Rapid urbanization and population growth have increased the demand for housing, especially in major cities like Harare and Bulawayo. The limited supply of quality housing options has driven up property prices in these urban areas.)
/E ( Urbanisation and Population Growth:    - Rapid urbanization and population growth have increased the demand for housing, especially in major cities like Harare and Bulawayo. The limited supply of quality housing options has driven up property prices in these urban areas.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 84 0 R
/T (Land Scarcity and Zoning Regulations:    - Land scarcity, combined with strict zoning regulations, has limited the availability of land for development, leading to increased competition for existing properties and driving prices higher.)
/E (Land Scarcity and Zoning Regulations:    - Land scarcity, combined with strict zoning regulations, has limited the availability of land for development, leading to increased competition for existing properties and driving prices higher.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 84 0 R
/T (Infrastructure Development:    - Investments in infrastructure development, such as road improvements and utilities, have enhanced the appeal of certain areas, leading to price appreciation in these localities.)
/E (Infrastructure Development:    - Investments in infrastructure development, such as road improvements and utilities, have enhanced the appeal of certain areas, leading to price appreciation in these localities.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 84 0 R
/T (Supply Chain Challenges:    - Challenges in the supply chain, including shortages of construction materials and skilled labor, have led to higher construction costs, which are passed on to buyers, contributing to price hikes.)
/E (Supply Chain Challenges:    - Challenges in the supply chain, including shortages of construction materials and skilled labor, have led to higher construction costs, which are passed on to buyers, contributing to price hikes.)
